    lines=['# Qwen3.5 direct geometry32: CPU scaffold only','','No Qwen generation, Student fit, new GT reader/scoring, package installation, extra download, waiter, model service or automatic continuation was started. The existing independent pinned Qwen3.5-9B download remains owned by its original service. count0 in this publication denotes engineering preparation, not completed scientific sources;32parents/128anchors are planned and CPU hash-bound.','','The prepared scope reuses exact prior32 exposed parents,128 T2 anchors, context4 and separate original anchor images. One proposed normalized0..1000 JSON protocol has its own parser, exact anchor binding and separate empty/invalid/no-target/abstention/truncation states. The downloaded native Jinja template closes thinking with enable_thinking=False; this CPU check is not a GPU instruction-following or coordinate qualification. The old R1 Transformers4.52.4 lacks qwen3_5; a separate compatible runtime, final native processor/video callback, real GPU coordinate/identity/resource qualification and actual runner/evaluator still require completion before science. The scaffolding contains guarded bridges to unchanged original OPD and D2 and complete-prediction requirements for scoring. Download completion does not authorize or automatically start them.','','Do not substitute a Qwen2.5/R1 pixel parser, patch14 grid or model. Actual Qwen3.5 patch16/merge2 processor resize/crop/padding, timestamps and coordinate behavior remain pending. BF16 native hybrid FP32 exceptions must be recorded, not cast away. No migration of Temporal Teacher, single-Teacher claim, model/Prompt/head/optimizer search or per-domain OPD/D2 combination. New execution requires an explicit scope/hash-bound permit, fresh resource/deadline lock, verified checkpoint and actual qualification.','','## Existing D1/D2 saved-scalar diagnostic','','All rows below use prior sealed results only, no new inference or GT evaluation. D1 uses original OPD; D2 uses its exact same references with parameter-free Source-relative propagation. Same T2 and all extreme sources remain. Difference is D2 minus D1.','','| Domain | Metric | Mean pp | Median pp | Min / max pp | + / − / neutral / unknown |','|---|---|---:|---:|---|---|']
    for r in diagnostic['summary']:
        lines.append(f"|{r['dataset']}|{r['metric']}|{r['mean_delta_pp']:.6f}|{r['median_delta_pp']:.6f}|{r['min_delta_pp']:.6f} / {r['max_delta_pp']:.6f}|{r['positive']}/{r['negative']}/{r['neutral']}/{r['unknown']}|")
    lines+=['','The HC vIoU mean is positive but spans large positive/negative source changes; Vid vIoU has median0 and a negative mean while dense/nonanchor means are positive. These are metric/support and distribution observations, not proof of a universally superior propagation rule or an instruction to remove extremes. Paired intervals and every anonymous source delta remain in the JSON. The new Qwen experiment will evaluate geometry coverage/quality, Full-minus-T2, nonanchor spatial quality, tails, same-reference OPD/D2 and real cost jointly; no rule requiring every development32 interval to exclude zero is introduced.','','CPU entry commands and the exact deferred DAG are in protocols/stvg_qwen35_geometry32_v1.md. No production CURRENT or frozen paper method was changed. Semantic512 remains a separate pending review; these plots do not supply identity/role labels.']
    doc=ROOT/'docs/STVG_QWEN35_GEOMETRY32_SCAFFOLD_001.md';doc.write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
    import matplotlib;matplotlib.use('Agg');import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
    fig,axs=plt.subplots(1,2,figsize=(10,3.8))
    for ax,ds in zip(axs,['hc2','vidstg']):
        values=[r['D2_minus_D1_pp'] for r in diagnostic['rows'] if r['dataset']==ds and r['metric']=='m_vIoU'];ax.bar(range(1,17),values);ax.axhline(0,color='black',lw=.7);ax.set_title(ds+' all16 parents (old results)');ax.set_xlabel('Fixed within-domain source order');ax.set_ylabel('D2 minus D1 vIoU (pp)')
    fig.tight_layout();fig.savefig(out/'saved_D1_D2_distribution.png',dpi=140);plt.close(fig)
    for name in ['stvg_qwen35_geometry32_v1.py','stvg_qwen35_geometry_contract_v1.py','stvg_qwen35_geometry_adapters_v1.py','test_stvg_qwen35_geometry_scaffold_v1.py','report_stvg_qwen35_geometry_scaffold_v1.py']:
        p=out/'code'/name;p.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True);p.write_text(public_source_text((ROOT/'scripts'/name).read_bytes()))
    paths={str(p.relative_to(ROOT)) for p in out.rglob('*') if p.is_file()}|{str(doc.relative_to(ROOT)),'protocols/stvg_qwen35_geometry32_v1.md'}
    verify_privacy(paths);write(BASE/'publication/scaffold/EXPORT_MANIFEST.json',dict(status='complete',count=0,scope='CPU scaffold and prior sealed scalar diagnostic; no Qwen science',paths=sorted(paths),files=[dict(path=p,sha256=sha(ROOT/p),bytes=(ROOT/p).stat().st_size) for p in sorted(paths)]));print('QWEN35_CPU_SCAFFOLD_EXPORT_READY',len(paths))
